# AGENTS.md

Architecture and working agreements for {{name}} (`{{id}}`), an Obsidian
plugin. Read this before adding features; commands and gate details live in
`CLAUDE.md` and `docs/quality-integration-guide.md`.

## Architecture

| Layer | Path                                                | Purpose                                                                                | May import                                             |
| ----- | --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| main  | `src/main.ts`, `src/settings.ts`, `src/commands.ts` | Plugin entry + registration. `main.ts` orchestrates only; `commands.ts` wires commands | core, ui                                               |
| core  | `src/core/`                                         | Provider-neutral services, no UI: commands, event bus, notices, modals                 | nothing app-internal (type-only edges to main allowed) |
| ui    | `src/ui/`                                           | Views, components, status bar                                                          | core (type-only edges to main allowed)                 |

These boundaries are **machine-enforced**: fallow's zone rules gate
`boundaryViolations` at 0 in `check:quality`. Keep core leaf-ward — a core
module that needs something from main/ui receives it as a constructor
argument or event, never as an import.

`main.ts` is orchestration-only: it constructs the services and delegates
every registration (`registerCommands`, `registerStatusBar`, `registerExtras`,
`registerActivity`{{registerViewsNote}}). Add new wiring as its own `register*`
module rather than growing `onload`. `registerExtras.ts` is a worked sample of two common
affordances — a ribbon icon that opens a `SuggestModal` picker
(`GreetingSuggestModal.ts`) and an `editor-menu` context item — kept UI-only
(the picker hands its choice back through a callback; state lands via
`saveSettings`).

## Services (owned by the plugin instance)

- **`plugin.commands` — `CommandsService`** (`src/core/commands/`): register
  commands through `addSimple` / `addChecked` / `addEditor` instead of calling
  `addCommand` directly. Command ids are **bare** — Obsidian prefixes the plugin
  id, and both the plugin id and the word "command" in an id are lint-banned;
  names are sentence case without the plugin name. All command wiring lives in
  `src/commands.ts`.
- **`plugin.events` — `EventBus<AppEvents>`** (`src/core/events/`): typed
  pub/sub scoped to the plugin. Add every event to the `AppEvents` map so
  payloads stay typed end-to-end. `on()` returns the unsubscribe function —
  always pair it with a lifecycle hook (`onUnmounted`, `onunload`).
- **`plugin.notices` — `NoticeService`** (`src/core/notices/`): the single
  seam for user-facing notices. Raw `new Notice()` is lint-banned outside the
  service; this keeps notices testable (the test double logs them), durations
  consistent, and gives i18n one place to land later. UI copy stays sentence
  case.
- **`plugin.modals` — `ModalService`** (`src/core/modals/`): async wrappers
  over Obsidian modals (`await plugin.modals.confirm(title, message)`).
  Extend it with new dialog kinds instead of scattering `Modal` subclasses.
- **`plugin.errors` — `ErrorService`** (`src/core/errors/`): the catch/log/notice
  seam. `run(context, op, opts?)` runs a fallible op and, on throw, logs via
  `Logger` and shows a notice (returning `undefined`); `wrap(context, fn, opts?)`
  wraps a callback so a throw or rejection never becomes a dead command. `opts`
  takes a user `message` and a `level` (`'warn'` for expected/transient failures
  like an offline check, `'error'` by default). `onload` and the network/vault
  command demos route through it — reach for this instead of a bare `try/catch`.
- **`plugin.ribbon` — `RibbonService`** (`src/core/ribbon/`): `add(icon, title, onClick)`
  over `addRibbonIcon`. Obsidian removes ribbon items on unload (no teardown); the
  returned element lets you toggle a state class. `registerExtras` uses it for the
  greeting picker.
- **`plugin.statusBar` — `StatusBarService`** (`src/core/statusbar/`): `add()`
  returns a chainable item handle (`setText`/`setTooltip`/`onClick`/`remove`).
  Clicks bind through `registerDomEvent`, so they are dropped on unload — never a
  raw `addEventListener`. `registerStatusBar` builds the greeting mirror with it.
- **`plugin.menus` — `MenuService`** (`src/core/menus/`): `onEditorMenu(cb)` /
  `onFileMenu(cb)` over the workspace context-menu events, registered through
  `registerEvent`. Build items in the handler with `menu.addItem(...)`;
  `registerExtras` adds both an editor and a file item.
- **`plugin.timers` — `TimersService`** (`src/core/timers/`): `every(ms, cb)` (a
  `registerInterval` Obsidian clears on unload) and `debounce(ms, fn)` (coalesce a
  burst — auto-save, search-as-you-type; pending timers are cleared on unload via
  `plugin.register`). Never a raw `setInterval`/`setTimeout` in feature code.
- **`plugin.vaultEvents` — `VaultEventsService`** (`src/core/vaultEvents/`): typed
  `onModify`/`onCreate`/`onDelete`/`onRename` over `vault.on(...)`, each through
  `registerEvent`. `registerActivity` reacts to all four (modify debounced).
- **`plugin.logger` — `Logger`** (`src/core/logging/`): the only sanctioned
  `console` user (raw `console.*` is lint-banned). `debug`/`info` are gated by
  the `debugLogging` setting; `warn`/`error` always print. `child('name')`
  namespaces a subsystem.
- **`plugin.vault` — `VaultService`** (`src/core/vault/`): Vault-API wrapper
  (preferred over the Adapter API) with `normalizePath` baked in —
  `ensureFolder` / `read` / `write` without hand-building paths.
- **`plugin.requests` — `RequestService`** (`src/core/http/`): wraps
  `requestUrl` (NOT `fetch`) so calls are CORS-safe and work on mobile.
- **Settings** are owned by `SettingsService` (`src/core/settings/`):
  `saveSettings(patch)` persists a partial change and emits `settings:changed`.
  Loading runs `migrateSettings` (`src/settings.ts`) so a vault on an old
  schema is upgraded, never broken — add a branch per `schemaVersion` bump.

### Editor-surface samples (`src/ui/`, wired by `registerEditorFeatures`)

Four common patterns you'll extend or delete — each keeps its testable logic in a
pure function so it unit-tests without an editor:

- **`EmojiSuggest`** — a `:shortcode` autocomplete (`EditorSuggest`). The match
  logic is the pure `emojiMatches(query)`.
- **`codeBlock`** — a reading-view renderer for fenced ` ```{{id}} ` blocks
  (`registerMarkdownCodeBlockProcessor`). `renderPanel(source, el)` builds the DOM.
- **`editorHighlight`** — a live TODO/FIXME/HACK highlighter (CodeMirror 6
  `ViewPlugin` via `registerEditorExtension`; `@codemirror/*` is external at
  runtime). The scan is the pure `markerRanges(text)`.
- A **"stamp modified date"** command writing note frontmatter through
  `plugin.vault.updateFrontmatter(path, patch)` (atomic `processFrontMatter`).

`main.ts` is orchestration-only: it constructs these services and wraps
`onload` in the `ErrorService` boundary (`this.errors.run('load the plugin', …)`)
— a thrown load reports via `logger` + `notices` and degrades, instead of
leaving Obsidian half-registered.

**i18n:** all user-facing text goes through `t('key')` (`src/i18n/`), backed by
`en.json`. A literal or template string passed to `plugin.notices.info/error`
is lint-banned — add a key and interpolate with `t('key', { name })`. Add
locales by keying on Obsidian's `getLanguage()` with an `en` fallback.

**`{{run}} verify`** runs the whole local gate chain in CI order — one command
before pushing. If you enabled the **opt-in** `.claude/` SessionStart hook at
scaffold time, it installs deps so a fresh Claude Code web session is ready.

## Commands (`src/commands.ts`)

Pick the helper by how the command should behave:

| Helper             | Obsidian mechanism    | Use when                                                     |
| ------------------ | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `addSimple`        | `callback`            | The command is always runnable.                              |
| `addChecked`       | `checkCallback`       | The command only applies in some state — it hides otherwise. |
| `addEditor`        | `editorCallback`      | The command acts on the active Markdown editor.              |
| `addEditorChecked` | `editorCheckCallback` | An editor command that is also conditional.                  |

`checkCallback`/`editorCheckCallback` are called twice: with `checking: true`
to ask "does this apply?" (return a boolean, do nothing) and `checking: false`
to run it. The `addChecked`/`addEditorChecked` wrappers collapse that into one
`when()` predicate plus a `run()`. Command ids are stable after release (they
key user hotkeys), and the service intentionally forbids caller-supplied
hotkeys — hardcoded defaults collide across plugins.

## Event flow (worked example)

Settings save → `saveSettings()` emits `settings:changed` on the bus → the
status-bar item and (Vue) the `useGreeting` composable update. Follow this
shape for new cross-cutting state: emit from the owner, subscribe where
rendered, unsubscribe on teardown (`onUnmounted` in components; plugin-lifetime
subscriptions like the status bar need no teardown — the bus dies on unload).

